      "title": "A. Reaction involving acidic hydrogen (Roman Urdu)",
      "language": "roman_ur",
      "variant_of": "C12-CHEM-CH23-23.5-A-REACTION-INVOLVING-ACIDIC-HYDROGEN",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "2d720c54-503b-58ec-b5b1-3307f222f40c",
          "pdf_from": 110,
          "pdf_to": 110,
          "note": "A. Reaction involving acidic hydrogen: a main subheading of 23.5 Reactions of Carboxylic Acids, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 110-110."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Carboxylic acids kafi acidic hain kyun ke paani mein H⁺ ions dete hain. Isi liye yeh basic cheezon (bases) aur active (tez react karne wali) metals se react karte hain."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "a) Active metals ke saath"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{2CH3-COOH + 2Na -> 2CH3-COO^-Na^+ + H2}",
            "text_alt": "2CH₃–COOH + 2Na → 2CH₃–COO⁻Na⁺ + H₂"
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "b) Alkalis ke saath"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3-COOH + NaOH -> CH3-COO^-Na^+ + H2O}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃–COOH + NaOH → CH₃–COO⁻Na⁺ + H₂O"
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "c) Metal carbonates aur bicarbonates ke saath (CO₂ ke bulbule nikalte hain)"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{2CH3-COOH + Na2CO3 -> 2CH3-COO^-Na^+ + CO2 + H2O}",
            "text_alt": "2CH₃–COOH + Na₂CO₃ → 2CH₃–COO⁻Na⁺ + CO₂ + H₂O"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3-COOH + NaHCO3 -> CH3-COO^-Na^+ + CO2 + H2O}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃–COOH + NaHCO₃ → CH₃–COO⁻Na⁺ + CO₂ + H₂O"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
